From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:53:28 +0800
Subject: upstream-pr-3037: Ocarina of Time renders taller screens natively
 (nxnative 47578ded)

Upstream's screen-shape stubs for Ocarina of Time (DM_SCREEN_ASPECT): taller render targets,
cameras at 16:9's sides with more above and below, the HUD and menus fitted to the height,
and the title and opening movies kept 16:9 inside the taller picture.

NXForge on top:
- the stubs sit beside NXForge's wide-screen, foliage, model detail, shadow cascade and 4K
  output stubs; upstream's 'graphics init' function is 'shape: graphics init' here, since
  NXForge's 4K output names another function so
- the loader gives a screen taller than 16:9 (the Mac's Aspect ratio row at 16:10, or Auto
  on a MacBook) to the shape stubs when the build has both (SCREEN_ASPECT capability), so
  16:10 no longer squeezes the HUD's 2D art; ultrawide stays with DM_SCREEN_WIDE
- Picture shape stays a row for the games whose profile has screen_aspect on; the tests
  count the shape's 19 hooks on top of NXForge's own

